+// stops at the cap without an error, so a zstd member whose content is larger was searched only
+// up to the cap. Ocarina of Time's /Shader/Model.Product.110.product.Nin_Ounce_NVN2.bfsha.zs
+// holds two BNSH, at 0xf7d000 (over 240 MiB long, so it never fit) and at 0x11543000 (277 MiB
+// in): 11,788 of the recipe's 41,216 programs, every one of them "not found". The offsets are
+// from nxnative's shader_map.tsv (github.com/seedds/nxnative, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds),
+// which names each program's file and BNSH. With the switch a cut is never silent: BNSH data over
+// the cap is inflated again in passes that keep only what the BNSH parser reads (headers,
+// variation tables, program and stage records, control sections), then a last pass cuts each
+// program's code as it streams by. Other content over the cap is an archive error. Peak memory is
+// the kept pieces plus a 4 MiB window, not MaxBlob.
+// EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_STREAM_VERIFY=1 (with the above): every BNSH member under the cap is also cut
+// the streamed way and the two compared (stage, fingerprint, origin); a difference is an archive
+// error, so the set is not stamped.
+// Both are read at first use: a namespace-scope value is set before main applies env.txt.
+bool StreamOn() {
